@startuml
title Idempotence - Double soumission d'une commande UC-05

autonumber
actor "Abonne / PME" as User
participant "API Gateway\nNGINX" as Gateway
participant "svc-commandes-activations\nPOST /v1/orders" as Orders
database "DB commandes_activations\norders" as OrderDb
participant "svc-clients-identite" as Customers
participant "svc-catalogue-offres" as Offers
participant "svc-conformite-audit" as Audit

== Premiere soumission ==

User -> Gateway : POST /v1/orders\nIdempotency-Key: abc-123\npayload A
Gateway -> Orders : forward
Orders -> Orders : calculer request_hash(payload A)
Orders -> OrderDb : find_order_by_idempotency_key(abc-123)
OrderDb --> Orders : aucune commande existante
Orders -> Customers : GET /v1/customers/{customerId}
Customers --> Orders : client ACTIVE,\nidentityStatus=VERIFIED,\nriskLevel=LOW
Orders -> Offers : GET /v1/offers/{offerId}
Offers --> Orders : offre ACTIVE, prix
Orders -> OrderDb : INSERT order\nidempotency_key=abc-123,\nrequest_hash,\nresponse_body,\nhttp_status=201
Orders -> Audit : POST /v1/audit-events\nORDER_ACCEPTED
Audit --> Orders : 201
Orders --> Gateway : 201 Created\nIdempotency-Replayed=false\norderId=ORD-001
Gateway --> User : 201 Created\ncommande acceptee

== Rejeu avec la meme cle et le meme payload ==

User -> Gateway : POST /v1/orders\nIdempotency-Key: abc-123\npayload A
Gateway -> Orders : forward
Orders -> Orders : calculer request_hash(payload A)
Orders -> OrderDb : find_order_by_idempotency_key(abc-123)
OrderDb --> Orders : order existante\nrequest_hash identique,\nresponse_body stocke,\nhttp_status=201
Orders --> Gateway : 201 stored response\nIdempotency-Replayed=true\norderId=ORD-001
Gateway --> User : 201 meme resultat\naucune nouvelle commande

== Rejeu avec la meme cle mais un payload different ==

User -> Gateway : POST /v1/orders\nIdempotency-Key: abc-123\npayload B
Gateway -> Orders : forward
Orders -> Orders : calculer request_hash(payload B)
Orders -> OrderDb : find_order_by_idempotency_key(abc-123)
OrderDb --> Orders : order existante\nrequest_hash different
Orders --> Gateway : 409 idempotency_key_conflict
Gateway --> User : 409 erreur JSON normalisee

note over Orders,OrderDb
La contrainte unique uq_orders_idempotency_key
protege la table contre les doublons.
Le request_hash distingue un rejeu identique
d'une reutilisation incorrecte de la meme cle.
end note

@enduml
